</style><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"ScholarlyArticle","headline":"State of AI Agent Security: The Tool Calls Arrive","description":"Issue 6 of the monthly Behavioral Threat Report. Synthesis of TrapMyAgent, AgentPwn, HoneyMap, and ARIAscout telemetry over the September 19 to October 19, 2026 (30 days) window, measured in one pass on October 19, 2026.","author":[{"@type":"Organization","name":"ARIA, OpenA2A autonomous research system","url":"https://research.opena2a.org"},{"@type":"Person","name":"Abdel Fane","affiliation":"OpenA2A Research"}],"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"OpenA2A","url":"https://opena2a.org","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://opena2a.org/logo.png"}},"datePublished":"2026-10-19","dateModified":"2026-10-27","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://research.opena2a.org/reports/state-of-ai-agent-security-2026-10"},"url":"https://research.opena2a.org/reports/state-of-ai-agent-security-2026-10","about":["AI agent security","Behavioral Threat Report","MCP","A2A","Agent Threat Matrix","Common Crawl gap","Indirect prompt injection","Agent attribution"],"isPartOf":{"@type":"PublicationIssue","issueNumber":"6","datePublished":"2026-10-19","isPartOf":{"@type":"Periodical","name":"Behavioral Threat Report"}},"citation":[{"@type":"CreativeWork","name":"Agent Threat Matrix","url":"https://threats.opena2a.org"},{"@type":"CreativeWork","name":"OASB - Open Agent Security Benchmark","url":"https://oasb.ai"}],"image":"https://opena2a.org/og-image.png"}</script><section class="relative flex min-h-0 flex-col justify-between gap-6 overflow-hidden pb-10 pt-7" style="background:#06070a;color:#e9eef4"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-40"><canvas class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full" aria-hidden="true"></canvas></div><div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-16" style="background:linear-gradient(180deg, #06070a 0%, #06070ad0 32%, transparent 100%)"></div><div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-9 h-19" style="background:linear-gradient(180deg, transparent 0%, #06070ab3 14%, #06070af2 30%, #06070a 42%)"></div><header class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-5 sm:px-6"><span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em]" style="font-family:var(--font-plex-mono), monospace;font-weight:700;color:#ffffff;text-shadow:0 1px 14px #06070a, 0 0 16px #06070a">October 19, 2026</span></header><div class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-5 sm:px-6"><p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em]" style="font-family:var(--font-plex-mono), monospace;color:#5fd0c6;text-shadow:0 1px 16px #06070a, 0 0 16px #06070a">Behavioral Threat Report. Issue 6.</p><h1 class="mt-3 text-[30px] leading-[1.08] md:text-[40px]" style="font-family:var(--font-newsreader), Georgia, serif;letter-spacing:-0.01em;font-weight:500;text-shadow:0 2px 24px #06070a">State of AI Agent Security<span class="sr-only">: </span><span class="block italic" style="color:#5fd0c6">The Tool Calls Arrive</span></h1></div></section><article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 pb-14"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-1 border-b pb-5 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em]" style="border-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.1);font-family:var(--font-plex-mono), monospace;color:rgba(233,238,244,0.78)"><span>Authored by ARIA.</span> <span>Edited by Abdel Fane.</span> <time dateTime="2026-10-19">Published <!-- -->October 19, 2026<!-- -->.</time> <span>7 min<!-- --> read.</span> <span><a href="#changes" data-corrected-link="" class="underline decoration-1 underline-offset-4 whitespace-nowrap hover:decoration-2">Updated <time dateTime="2026-10-27">October 27, 2026</time></a>.</span></div><div class="mt-3 text-[12px] tracking-wide" style="font-family:var(--font-plex-mono), monospace;color:rgba(233,238,244,0.62)" data-edition-dataline="">30-day window September 19 to October 19, 2026, closed at 00:00 UTC. Measured October 19, 2026.</div><p class="mt-9 first-letter:float-left first-letter:mr-2.5 first-letter:text-[clamp(34px,8.5vw,42px)] first-letter:font-semibold first-letter:leading-[0.78]" style="color:rgba(233,238,244,0.92)">The clients reaching TrapMyAgent&#x27;s decoy MCP servers asked them to do things this window:<!-- --> <strong style="color:#fff">420</strong> tool calls, from <!-- -->19<!-- --> <!-- -->fingerprints. Nothing that fetched an injected link on the AgentPwn pages declared itself an agent, and something is walking our Agent-to-Agent endpoints and stopping at the handshake.</p><section class="mt-12 mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-5 text-white">This month in numbers</h2><div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-6 gap-y-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><div class="border-t border-white/15 pt-3"><div class="text-2xl text-white" style="font-family:var(--font-newsreader), Georgia, serif;line-height:1">420</div><div class="text-[12px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 mt-1.5 font-mono">MCP tool calls on TrapMyAgent&#x27;s decoy servers</div><div class="text-[12px] text-gray-400 mt-1 font-mono">from 19 fingerprints</div></div><div class="border-t border-white/15 pt-3"><div class="text-2xl text-white" style="font-family:var(--font-newsreader), Georgia, serif;line-height:1">2,578 / 235 / 0</div><div class="text-[12px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 mt-1.5 font-mono">callbacks by declared client class: browser / crawler / agent</div><div class="text-[12px] text-gray-400 mt-1 font-mono">of 2,813 attributed AgentPwn callbacks</div></div><div class="border-t border-white/15 pt-3"><div class="text-2xl text-white" style="font-family:var(--font-newsreader), Georgia, serif;line-height:1">27,247</div><div class="text-[12px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 mt-1.5 font-mono">A2A handshakes</div><div class="text-[12px] text-gray-400 mt-1 font-mono">6.4% of TrapMyAgent events</div></div><div class="border-t border-white/15 pt-3"><div class="text-2xl text-white" style="font-family:var(--font-newsreader), Georgia, serif;line-height:1">2,495</div><div class="text-[12px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 mt-1.5 font-mono">exposed MCP servers</div><div class="text-[12px] text-gray-400 mt-1 font-mono">up from 1,997 on September 1, 48 days earlier</div></div><div class="border-t border-white/15 pt-3"><div class="text-2xl text-white" style="font-family:var(--font-newsreader), Georgia, serif;line-height:1">255,582</div><div class="text-[12px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 mt-1.5 font-mono">exposed AI services</div><div class="text-[12px] text-gray-400 mt-1 font-mono">ARIAscout sweep of October 19; no trend on the total</div></div></div></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Key findings</h2><ol class="space-y-4 ml-5 list-decimal"><li><strong class="text-white">The tool calls arrived.</strong> <!-- -->TrapMyAgent&#x27;s decoy MCP servers took <!-- -->420<!-- --> tool calls from <!-- -->19<!-- --> <!-- -->fingerprints, against <!-- -->396,401<!-- --> connection events. The call is the action, so alert on it rather than on the connection, and read every one.</li><li><strong class="text-white">Nothing that follows the bait identifies as an agent.</strong> <!-- -->All <!-- -->2,813<!-- --> attributed AgentPwn callbacks carry a verdict: <!-- -->2,578<!-- --> <!-- -->browsers and link previewers, <!-- -->235<!-- --> declared content crawlers, <!-- -->0<!-- --> generic HTTP clients and<!-- --> <!-- -->0<!-- --> declared autonomous agents. Attribute each fetch and take your own probes out before you publish a rate.</li><li><strong class="text-white">Something is still enumerating A2A endpoints.</strong> <!-- -->Handshakes totaled <!-- -->27,247<!-- -->, <!-- -->6.4<!-- -->% of TrapMyAgent events, and the task step that follows a handshake happened once. Authenticate the handshake now, while the traffic is still only knocking.</li><li><strong class="text-white">Exposed MCP servers grew <!-- -->24.9<!-- -->% in <!-- -->48<!-- --> days.</strong> <!-- -->The <!-- -->October 19<!-- --> sweep counted <!-- -->2,495<!-- -->, up from <!-- -->1,997<!-- --> on<!-- --> <!-- -->September 1<!-- -->, and OpenClaw gateways are <!-- -->80.5<!-- -->% of the<!-- --> <!-- -->255,582<!-- --> exposed AI services, a total we publish without a trend. Put a scoped credential in front of every endpoint you run.</li></ol></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">1. The tool calls arrived</h2><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">TrapMyAgent&#x27;s decoy MCP servers took <!-- -->420<!-- --> tool calls this window, from<!-- --> <!-- -->19<!-- --> distinct fingerprints, against <!-- -->396,401<!-- --> connection events. That distinction is the finding: a connection is a knock, a resource read is one step past it and still short of an action, and a tool call is the action.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">The calls arrived at a near daily cadence from September 26, which reads as scheduled tooling rather than a population of operators, so we publish the total and the fingerprint count and nothing per client. The tools asked for were log search, shell execution, database query, file read, secret fetch and user lookup, which is the set an operator tries first on an unfamiliar server. Two event types also appeared for the first time this window, a credential access and a soul probe, and both sit inside the small event types row because each stands on fewer than ten sources.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">Every tool call rides on a connection that already exists, so an alert on the call misses nothing an alert on the connection would catch, and it skips the crawler noise. If your MCP server is meant to sit idle, make the first tool call it receives page someone, whoever sent it, and treat the connection count as a crawler meter.</p><div class="border-l-2 border-teal-500/40 pl-4 mb-6"><h3 id="mcp-priority" class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2 scroll-mt-20"><a href="#mcp-priority" class="hover:text-teal-300">Alert on the tool call, not the connection.</a></h3><p class="text-sm text-gray-300 mb-2">A connection threshold is tuned to crawler behavior, so it pages you on indexing. A tool call to an MCP server that should be idle is the event worth a human, and this window&#x27;s count is still small enough that one person can read every call. Log the tool name and the arguments beside the connection, and read them.</p><p class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">Maps to:<!-- --> <span><a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-1002" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-1002</a></span><span>, <a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-2005" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-2005</a></span> · <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/2.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->2.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Explicit Capability Grants<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/2.3" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->2.3</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Capability Boundaries<!-- -->)</span></a></span></p></div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">Few MCP connections went on to a tool call</h3><div class="space-y-2"><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">events in this window</span><span class="font-mono text-white">425,975</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:100.00%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">MCP connections</span><span class="font-mono text-white">396,401</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:93.06%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">A2A handshakes</span><span class="font-mono text-white">27,247</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:6.40%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">context reads</span><span class="font-mono text-white">1,857</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.44%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">MCP resource reads</span><span class="font-mono text-white">34</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.01%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">MCP tool calls</span><span class="font-mono text-white">420</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.10%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">A2A tasks</span><span class="font-mono text-white">1</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.00%"></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">2. Nothing that follows the bait identifies as an agent</h2><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">A callback fires when a client fetches the URL inside an injection payload on an AgentPwn page, and every one of the <!-- -->2,813<!-- --> callbacks this window carries a client class verdict. Of those,<!-- --> <!-- -->2,578<!-- --> were browsers and link prefetchers, <!-- -->235<!-- --> declared themselves LLM content crawlers, <!-- -->0<!-- --> were generic HTTP clients and <!-- -->0<!-- --> declared themselves autonomous agents. The count carries no trend, because this edition excludes our own diagnostic probe and the previous window&#x27;s figure still carried its rows.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">A browser or an unfurler fetches every link it sees, so a callback proves a fetch, not a reading. The<!-- --> <!-- -->20<!-- --> baseline honeypots that drew traffic are built to be visible to crawlers, and visible surfaces draw crawlers. <!-- -->47<!-- --> callbacks reached the verified tier, every one a declared crawler whose network ownership matched its declaration, and a verified crawler is still a crawler, so no vendor is named as an actor. The claimed tier also has a blind spot the zero can&#x27;t close: an agent driving a real browser presents as that browser.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">If you run bait of your own, the probe exclusion is the step most teams skip. A diagnostic request from your own tooling lands in the same table as a crawler&#x27;s, and nothing labels it unless you do, so tag your own traffic at the source, attribute what remains, and only then count.</p><div class="border-l-2 border-teal-500/40 pl-4 mb-6"><h3 id="attribute-before-you-count" class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2 scroll-mt-20"><a href="#attribute-before-you-count" class="hover:text-teal-300">Attribute before you count.</a></h3><p class="text-sm text-gray-300 mb-2">Log the client class beside every fetch of an injected URL before you derive a rate from it, and take your own probes out of the count. A callback rate published without that split measures link unfurling, not agent compliance.</p><p class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">Maps to:<!-- --> <span><a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-2002" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-2002</a></span> · <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/10.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->10.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Security Event Logging<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/3.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->3.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Prompt Injection Protection<!-- -->)</span></a></span></p></div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">Every attributed callback declared a browser or a crawler</h3><div class="space-y-2"><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Browsers and link prefetchers<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">unfurlers, previewers</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">2,578</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-rose-400/70" style="width:100.00%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Declared LLM content crawlers<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">index pages, act on nothing</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">235</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-rose-400/70" style="width:9.12%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Generic HTTP clients<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">library user agents</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">0</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-rose-400/70" style="width:0.00%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Autonomous LLM agents<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">acting on tool output</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">0</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-rose-400/70" style="width:0.00%"></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">3. Something is still enumerating A2A endpoints</h2><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">TrapMyAgent recorded <!-- -->27,247<!-- --> Agent-to-Agent handshakes this window,<!-- --> <!-- -->6.4<!-- -->% of everything it recorded. The step after a handshake, where one agent asks another to do something, happened <!-- -->once<!-- -->.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">That shape is enumeration rather than use. Something is walking our A2A endpoints and stopping at the door, and because TrapMyAgent records the handshake and not the intent, we can&#x27;t say who or why. The public target set is small: the Registry&#x27;s <!-- -->October 19<!-- --> sweep found <!-- -->37<!-- --> <!-- -->A2A endpoints reachable on the open internet, against <!-- -->32<!-- --> on <!-- -->September 1<!-- -->, which at counts this small is a snapshot and not a trend.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">The handshake is the cheapest step for a scanner and the one step you can gate without touching the task path. An agent card is discoverable by design, so the enumeration itself isn&#x27;t the problem; the problem is an endpoint that accepts a task from any peer that completed a handshake. Gate the handshake now, while the traffic is still only knocking, and a walk of your endpoint list becomes a log of failed authentications you can read and a rate you can alert on.</p><div class="border-l-2 border-teal-500/40 pl-4 mb-6"><h3 id="a2a-woke-up" class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2 scroll-mt-20"><a href="#a2a-woke-up" class="hover:text-teal-300">Authenticate A2A handshakes now, not when they carry tasks.</a></h3><p class="text-sm text-gray-300 mb-2">If you expose an A2A endpoint, put mutual authentication and message integrity on the handshake while the traffic reaching it is still only knocking, and accept no task from a peer that hasn&#x27;t authenticated.</p><p class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">Maps to:<!-- --> <span><a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-1006" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-1006</a></span><span>, <a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-2008" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-2008</a></span><span>, <a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-3001" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-3001</a></span> · <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/7.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->7.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Mutual Authentication<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/7.2" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->7.2</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Message Integrity<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/5.2" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->5.2</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Context Window Isolation<!-- -->)</span></a></span></p></div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">A2A handshakes took a larger share of TrapMyAgent events</h3><div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 items-center mb-4"><div class="md:w-1/3 flex justify-center"><div class="flex flex-col items-center"><svg width="200" height="200" viewBox="0 0 200 200" role="img" aria-label="distribution donut chart"><path d="M 100 12 A 88 88 0 1 1 62.8185305545146 20.240747684833238 L 76.94748894379904 50.5492635645966 A 54.56 54.56 0 1 0 100 45.44 Z" class="fill-teal-400/85"></path><path d="M 62.8185305545146 20.240747684833238 A 88 88 0 0 1 96.98012105110898 12.051831564642328 L 98.12767505168756 45.47213557007824 A 54.56 54.56 0 0 0 76.94748894379904 50.5492635645966 Z" class="fill-amber-400/85"></path><path d="M 96.98012105110898 12.051831564642328 A 88 88 0 0 1 99.38993963797344 12.00211464839235 L 99.62176257554353 45.44131108200326 A 54.56 54.56 0 0 0 98.12767505168756 45.47213557007824 Z" class="fill-slate-400/85"></path><path d="M 99.38993963797344 12.00211464839235 A 88 88 0 0 1 99.99999999999999 12 L 99.99999999999999 45.44 A 54.56 54.56 0 0 0 99.62176257554353 45.44131108200326 Z" class="fill-sky-400/85"></path><text x="100" y="100" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" class="fill-white" style="font-size:45.945263157894736px;font-family:var(--font-newsreader), Georgia, serif">93%</text></svg><p class="mt-3 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 text-center max-w-[12rem] font-mono">MCP</p></div></div><div class="flex-1"><ul class="space-y-2 text-sm"><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-teal-400/85"></span><span class="text-gray-300 flex-1">Model Context Protocol (MCP) connection</span><span class="font-mono text-white">396,401</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-xs w-12 text-right">93.1<!-- -->%</span></li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-amber-400/85"></span><span class="text-gray-300 flex-1">Agent-to-Agent (A2A) handshake</span><span class="font-mono text-white">27,247</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-xs w-12 text-right">6.4<!-- -->%</span></li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-slate-400/85"></span><span class="text-gray-300 flex-1">Context read (other)</span><span class="font-mono text-white">1,857</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-xs w-12 text-right">0.4<!-- -->%</span></li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-sky-400/85"></span><span class="text-gray-300 flex-1">MCP resource read, file read, MCP tool call, credential access, soul probe, A2A task</span><span class="font-mono text-white">470</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-xs w-12 text-right">0.1<!-- -->%</span></li></ul></div></div></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">4. Exposed MCP servers grew <!-- -->24.9<!-- -->% in <!-- -->48<!-- --> days</h2><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">The Registry&#x27;s <!-- -->October 19<!-- --> sweep counted <!-- -->2,495<!-- --> exposed MCP servers, up from <!-- -->1,997<!-- --> on <!-- -->September 1<!-- -->, a rise of <!-- -->24.9<!-- -->% on the same query set. The interval is <!-- -->48<!-- --> days rather than a month because this edition&#x27;s sweep ran on the measurement date instead of the first of the month. OpenClaw gateways rose to<!-- --> <!-- -->205,638<!-- --> from <!-- -->192,492<!-- --> over the same interval and are <!-- -->80.5<!-- -->% of the <!-- -->255,582<!-- --> exposed AI services the sweep found.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">The total itself carries no trend. The LLM serving category inside it went from <!-- -->20,026<!-- --> to<!-- --> <!-- -->17,090<!-- --> and is published without a trend because it has swung on unchanged queries before, so the total&#x27;s change is stated net of that category:<!-- --> <!-- -->6.7<!-- -->% since <!-- -->September 1<!-- -->. Exposure counts reachable servers, while TrapMyAgent watches a set of decoy ones, and this window the traffic reaching the decoys asked them to do things. We can&#x27;t read the decoy traffic onto the exposed population, but a server that answers without a credential is one the next sweep will find in the same pass.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">Start with the list rather than with a control: enumerate every model endpoint, gateway and MCP server you run that answers without a credential, because that list is what the sweep finds and it&#x27;s the one to empty first.</p><div class="border-l-2 border-teal-500/40 pl-4 mb-6"><h3 id="exposed-inference" class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2 scroll-mt-20"><a href="#exposed-inference" class="hover:text-teal-300">Lock down unauthenticated model serving and gateway infrastructure.</a></h3><p class="text-sm text-gray-300 mb-2">Put a credential in front of every model endpoint and gateway, and scope that credential to the capability it needs. If you can&#x27;t say which of your endpoints answer without one, run the query the sweep runs and find out before someone else does.</p><p class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">Maps to:<!-- --> <span><a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-1002" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-1002</a></span> · <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/2.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->2.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Explicit Capability Grants<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/5.3" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->5.3</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Credential Scope Limitation<!-- -->)</span></a></span></p></div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">OpenClaw gateways are most of the exposed surface; MCP servers grew most since <!-- -->September 1</h3><div class="space-y-2"><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Exposed AI services<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">243,615 on September 1; no trend claim</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">255,582</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-amber-400/70" style="width:100.00%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">OpenClaw gateways<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">up 6.8% from 192,492</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">205,638</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-amber-400/70" style="width:80.46%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">LLM serving<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">20,026 on September 1; no trend claim</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">17,090</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-amber-400/70" style="width:6.69%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">MCP servers<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">up 24.9% from 1,997</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">2,495</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-amber-400/70" style="width:0.98%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">A2A endpoints<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">32 on September 1; snapshot</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">37</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-amber-400/70" style="width:0.01%"></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">What to do this month</h2><ol class="space-y-2 ml-5 list-decimal"><li>Alert on the MCP tool call, not the connection, and read every call a server that should be idle receives.<!-- --> <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">(<!-- -->finding 1<!-- -->;<!-- --> <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/2.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->2.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Explicit Capability Grants<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/2.3" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->2.3</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Capability Boundaries<!-- -->)</span></a></span>)</span></li><li>Log the client class beside every fetch of an injected URL, and take your own probes out of the count before you derive a rate.<!-- --> <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">(<!-- -->finding 2<!-- -->;<!-- --> <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/10.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->10.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Security Event Logging<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/3.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->3.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Prompt Injection Protection<!-- -->)</span></a></span>)</span></li><li>Put mutual authentication and message integrity on every A2A handshake, and accept no task from a peer that hasn&#x27;t authenticated.<!-- --> <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">(<!-- -->finding 3<!-- -->;<!-- --> <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/7.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->7.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Mutual Authentication<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/7.2" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->7.2</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Message Integrity<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/5.2" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->5.2</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Context Window Isolation<!-- -->)</span></a></span>)</span></li><li>Put a scoped credential in front of every model endpoint, gateway and MCP server you run.<!-- --> <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">(<!-- -->finding 4<!-- -->;<!-- --> <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/2.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->2.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Explicit Capability Grants<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/5.3" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->5.3</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Credential Scope Limitation<!-- -->)</span></a></span>)</span></li><li>Split recurrence by classifier verdict before you read it as persistence, and stop comparing across an identifier change.<!-- --> <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">(<!-- -->Appendix A<!-- -->;<!-- --> <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/10.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->10.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Security Event Logging<!-- -->)</span></a></span>)</span></li><li>Strip hidden text, HTML comments, script literals and tag block Unicode from retrieved web content before it reaches the context.<!-- --> <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">(<!-- -->Appendix A<!-- -->;<!-- --> <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/3.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->3.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Prompt Injection Protection<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/3.3" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->3.3</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Input Validation<!-- -->)</span></a></span>)</span></li><li>Instrument authenticated and dynamic surfaces before you draw conclusions about agents from crawl data.<!-- --> <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">(<!-- -->Methodology<!-- -->; no control mapping<!-- -->)</span></li></ol></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">What we can&#x27;t say yet</h2><ul class="space-y-2 ml-4 list-disc"><li>Whether any agent has acted on an injection: the authenticated cohort that could observe one recorded no interactions, no FOITW signature fired in the window, a claimed tier verdict can&#x27;t separate an agent driving a real browser from the browser, and our own test traffic and our own probe are excluded from every count.</li><li>A page level agent share: attribution is wired on <!-- -->4.5<!-- -->% of AgentPwn rows while the per surface rollout completes, so callbacks are the only attributed population.</li><li>Who is enumerating A2A endpoints: TrapMyAgent records the handshake, not the intent.</li><li>A trend on the LLM serving exposure category, or on the exposed AI services total it moves: the category has swung on unchanged queries before.</li><li>Any vendor as an actor: <!-- -->47<!-- --> callbacks reached the verified tier, all declared crawlers, and the other <!-- -->2,766<!-- --> are claimed tier.</li><li>A trend on fingerprints or recurrence: TrapMyAgent changed how it identifies a client inside the window, so the <!-- -->11,321<!-- --> distinct fingerprints and the <!-- -->3,427<!-- --> seen in more than one session are counts, not a comparison.</li></ul></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">Bottom line</h2><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">Some of what arrived acted. Clients connected to our decoy MCP servers and then asked them to do things, the Agent-to-Agent handshakes had almost no task behind them, and nothing that fetched our bait declared itself an agent. A connection count tells you who is indexing; a tool call tells you who is trying. So start with one MCP server you run, list every tool call it received in the last thirty days, and alert on the next one.</p></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">Methodology and data</h2><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3"><strong class="text-white">Window.</strong> <!-- -->September 19 to October 19, 2026 (30 days)<!-- -->, measured in one pass on<!-- --> <!-- -->October 19, 2026<!-- -->; the <!-- -->October 19<!-- --> exposure sweep ran inside that pass. Given here once:<!-- --> <!-- -->30-day window September 19 to October 19, 2026, closed at 00:00 UTC. Measured October 19, 2026.<!-- --> TrapMyAgent time is capture time, not ingest time.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3"><strong class="text-white">Streams.</strong> <!-- -->TrapMyAgent&#x27;s honey agents record protocol level events from whatever connects: the request, not the intent. AgentPwn&#x27;s honeypot pages carry benign injection payloads and record visits and callbacks. HoneyMap samples the public web for third party bait, not a coverage count. ARIAscout reads the Registry&#x27;s <!-- -->October 19<!-- --> exposure sweep: reachable, not attacked.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3"><strong class="text-white">Denominators.</strong> TrapMyAgent shares use the window event count,<!-- --> <!-- -->425,975<!-- -->; classifier shares use sessions, <!-- -->36,629<!-- -->; callback shares use the <!-- -->2,813<!-- --> attributed callbacks. The cumulative count,<!-- --> <!-- -->1,840,440<!-- -->, is never a denominator.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3"><strong class="text-white">Comparison basis.</strong> Issue 5, whose window closed on <!-- -->September 17<!-- -->, two days before this one opened: month over month, same instrument, same query, unless a note below withholds the trend. Exposure compares with Issue 5&#x27;s <!-- -->September 1<!-- --> sweep, <!-- -->48<!-- --> days before this edition&#x27;s, so no exposure change in this report is a monthly one.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3" id="withheld-breakdowns-note"><strong class="text-white">What changed since Issue 5.</strong> AgentPwn figures exclude our own diagnostic probe; the previous window&#x27;s callbacks carried its rows, so AgentPwn counts carry no trend. TrapMyAgent&#x27;s fingerprint and session identifier scheme changed on September 28, inside the window: no trend on distinct fingerprints or the returning share, while event and session totals are the same query over the same rows. APT reconnaissance stood on fewer than ten sources and shares a cell with manual researcher. Two new event types, credential access and soul probe, sit in the small types row. MCP tool calls are published as a total and a fingerprint count only. Five HoneyMap surfaces left the census after three removal observations each, and three were reclassified as false positives. The exposure sweep ran on the measurement date rather than the first of the month; both sweeps ran in the same detail mode over the same 33 query set, categories add to the total plus a credential category it leaves out, and LLM serving has swung on unchanged queries before, so it carries no trend. The AgentPwn category, ATT&amp;CK, country and cloud provider breakdowns are withheld: a row needs a recorded count of distinct client addresses at or above the floor, and none exists for this edition.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3"><strong class="text-white">Attribution tiers.</strong> Observed: we counted it. Claimed: the client declared it. Verified: network ownership matches the declaration; nothing lifts a verdict further yet. Network figures read as fronted through, never as originating in.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">Full methodology:<!-- --> <a class="text-teal-300 hover:underline" href="/methodology">/methodology</a>,<!-- --> <a class="text-teal-300 hover:underline" href="/methodology/behavioral-sweep">behavioral-sweep</a> <!-- -->and<!-- --> <a class="text-teal-300 hover:underline" href="/methodology/foitw">foitw</a>.</p><h3 class="text-base font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-white">How to cite</h3><div class="bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded p-3 font-mono text-xs mb-3 overflow-x-auto"><div class="text-gray-400 mb-2"># BibTeX</div><pre class="text-white whitespace-pre-wrap rw-code-wrap">@techreport{opena2a-btr-2026-10,
  author = {{ARIA, OpenA2A autonomous research system} and Abdel Fane (editor)},
  title  = {State of AI Agent Security: The Tool Calls Arrive},
  institution = {OpenA2A Research},
  year   = {2026},
  month  = {10},
  type   = {Behavioral Threat Report},
  number = {Issue 6},
  url    = {https://research.opena2a.org/reports/state-of-ai-agent-security-2026-10}
}</pre></div><div class="bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded p-3 font-mono text-xs mb-3 overflow-x-auto"><div class="text-gray-400 mb-2"># APA</div><pre class="text-white whitespace-pre-wrap rw-code-wrap">ARIA, &amp; Fane, A. (Ed.). (2026, October 19). State of AI Agent Security: The Tool Calls Arrive (Behavioral Threat Report, Issue 6). OpenA2A Research. https://research.opena2a.org/reports/state-of-ai-agent-security-2026-10</pre></div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2 text-white">How to challenge a finding</h3><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Email <a href="mailto:[email withheld by Lighthouse]" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline">[email withheld by Lighthouse]</a> <!-- -->with the number you dispute and the methodology you would prefer. We aim to respond within five business days, and challenges that hold up under review are published as methodology updates in later editions, with attribution.</p></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">Appendix A: Full tables</h2><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">Volume across the four streams</h3><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">The exposure row is the Registry&#x27;s <!-- -->October 19<!-- --> sweep. The AgentPwn rows are published without a trend this window because the previous window&#x27;s figures carried our own probe&#x27;s rows.</p><div class="space-y-2"><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">ARIAscout exposed AI services<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">Shodan sweep of October 19</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">255,582</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:60.00%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">TrapMyAgent events<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">honey agent observations</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">425,975</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:100.00%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">AgentPwn page interactions<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">honeypot pages</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">321,505</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:75.48%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">TrapMyAgent sessions</span><span class="font-mono text-white">36,629</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:8.60%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">AgentPwn payload callbacks<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">clients that fetched</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">2,813</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:0.66%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">HoneyMap wild bait surfaces<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">public web</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">292</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:0.07%"></div></div></div></div></div><div id="breakdowns-withheld" data-withheld-block="" class="scroll-mt-20 border-l-2 border-white/15 pl-4 my-6"><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Breakdowns withheld</h3><div><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-300 mb-2">Each row in these breakdowns needs ten or more distinct client addresses; that could not be confirmed.</p><ul role="list" class="list-none p-0 m-0 mb-3 space-y-1 text-sm text-gray-300"><li>AgentPwn payloads by category</li><li>Heuristic matches by ATT&amp;CK ID</li><li>Events by country</li><li>Events by cloud provider</li></ul></div><p class="text-sm"><a href="#withheld-breakdowns-note" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline">Why these breakdowns are withheld</a></p></div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">Almost every TrapMyAgent session is an automated scanner</h3><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">Of <!-- -->36,629<!-- --> sessions, <!-- -->34,710<!-- --> classify as automated scanners, <!-- -->94.8<!-- -->%, <!-- -->1,820<!-- --> <!-- -->as unknown and <!-- -->99<!-- --> as manual researcher or APT reconnaissance, two verdicts in one cell because the second stood on fewer than ten sources. A class that size is a set of flags to read by hand, not a noise floor. <!-- -->3,427<!-- --> of <!-- -->11,321<!-- --> <!-- -->distinct fingerprints appeared in more than one session, a count with no comparison because the identifier scheme changed inside the window.</p><div class="mb-3 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-6"><div class="md:w-48 shrink-0 flex justify-center"><div class="flex flex-col items-center"><svg width="180" height="180" viewBox="0 0 180 180" role="img" aria-label="distribution donut chart"><path d="M 90 12 A 78 78 0 1 1 64.78536591233484 16.187926273372085 L 74.3669268656476 44.23651428949069 A 48.36 48.36 0 1 0 90 41.64 Z" class="fill-rose-400/85"></path><path d="M 64.78536591233484 16.187926273372085 A 78 78 0 0 1 88.67546411524565 12.01124693463808 L 89.17878775145229 41.64697309947561 A 48.36 48.36 0 0 0 74.3669268656476 44.23651428949069 Z" class="fill-slate-400/85"></path><path d="M 88.67546411524565 12.01124693463808 A 78 78 0 0 1 89.99999999999999 12 L 89.99999999999999 41.64 A 48.36 48.36 0 0 0 89.17878775145229 41.64697309947561 Z" class="fill-amber-400/85"></path><text x="90" y="90" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" class="fill-white" style="font-size:28.46608695652174px;font-family:var(--font-newsreader), Georgia, serif">94.8%</text></svg><p class="mt-3 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 text-center max-w-[12rem] font-mono">Automated scanner</p></div></div><div class="flex-1"><ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm"><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-rose-400/85"></span><span class="text-gray-300 flex-1">Automated scanner</span><span class="font-mono text-white">34,710</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-xs w-12 text-right">94.8<!-- -->%</span></li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-slate-400/85"></span><span class="text-gray-300 flex-1">Unknown</span><span class="font-mono text-white">1,820</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-xs w-12 text-right">5.0<!-- -->%</span></li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-amber-400/85"></span><span class="text-gray-300 flex-1">Manual researcher or APT reconnaissance</span><span class="font-mono text-white">99</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-xs w-12 text-right">0.3<!-- -->%</span></li></ul></div></div><div class="mt-6"><div class="border-l-2 border-teal-500/40 pl-4 mb-6"><h3 id="persistence" class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2 scroll-mt-20"><a href="#persistence" class="hover:text-teal-300">Segment out scanners before you call anything persistence.</a></h3><p class="text-sm text-gray-300 mb-2">A returning visitor figure that doesn&#x27;t first remove the scanner class measures scanner scheduling, not adversary persistence. Keep the fingerprint and session log, split it by classifier verdict, and read recurrence inside each class. And when your sensor changes how it identifies a client, as ours did this window, stop comparing recurrence across the change.</p><p class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">Maps to:<!-- --> <span><a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-9001" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-9001</a></span> · <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/10.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->10.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Security Event Logging<!-- -->)</span></a></span></p></div></div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">HoneyMap: injection bait planted on the public web</h3><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">A sample, not a coverage count. At measurement the catalog held <!-- -->292<!-- --> surfaces across<!-- --> <!-- -->239<!-- --> unique domains, against <!-- -->276<!-- --> surfaces and <!-- -->226<!-- --> <!-- -->domains last window on the same signature set. The Unicode tag block class kept growing, to<!-- --> <!-- -->69<!-- --> surfaces from <!-- -->54<!-- -->, and script literals as a placement went from <!-- -->32<!-- --> surfaces to <!-- -->47<!-- -->. <!-- -->273<!-- --> of the<!-- --> <!-- -->292<!-- --> surfaces carry no sector classification because the catalog doesn&#x27;t guess one. Hidden text and HTML comments still hold most of the bait, but the growth this window is in tag block Unicode and script literals, which a filter that only strips hidden elements and comments will miss.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-2">Attack classes:</p><div class="space-y-2"><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">SOUL-INJECT<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">Indirect prompt injection (T-2002)</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">223</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-rose-400/70" style="width:100.00%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">UNICODE-STEGO<span class="text-gray-400 ml-2">Indirect prompt injection (T-2002)</span></span><span class="font-mono text-white">69</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-rose-400/70" style="width:30.94%"></div></div></div></div></div><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-6 mb-2">Top AIIS signatures observed:</p><div class="space-y-2"><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">AIIS-HIDDEN-JAILBREAK-DAN-01</span><span class="font-mono text-white">119</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-rose-400/70" style="width:100.00%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">AIIS-HIDDEN-ROLE-INJECT-01</span><span class="font-mono text-white">85</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-rose-400/70" style="width:71.43%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">AIIS-UNICODE-TAG-BLOCK-01</span><span class="font-mono text-white">69</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-rose-400/70" style="width:57.98%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">AIIS-ATTR-IGNORE-INST-01</span><span class="font-mono text-white">19</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-rose-400/70" style="width:15.97%"></div></div></div></div></div><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-6 mb-2">Where the bait lives on the page:</p><div class="space-y-2"><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Hidden text (display:none, visibility:hidden)</span><span class="font-mono text-white">154</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:100.00%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">HTML comment</span><span class="font-mono text-white">59</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:38.31%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Script literal (embedded in JS)</span><span class="font-mono text-white">47</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:30.52%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Alt and ARIA attributes</span><span class="font-mono text-white">17</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:11.04%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Meta tags</span><span class="font-mono text-white">8</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:5.19%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Data attributes</span><span class="font-mono text-white">7</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-teal-400/70" style="width:4.55%"></div></div></div></div></div><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-6 mb-2">Sector distribution:</p><div class="space-y-2"><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Unknown</span><span class="font-mono text-white">273</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:100.00%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">News</span><span class="font-mono text-white">8</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:2.93%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Blog</span><span class="font-mono text-white">2</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.73%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Ecommerce</span><span class="font-mono text-white">2</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.73%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Forum</span><span class="font-mono text-white">2</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.73%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Academic</span><span class="font-mono text-white">1</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.37%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Social</span><span class="font-mono text-white">1</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.37%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Sports</span><span class="font-mono text-white">1</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.37%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Tech</span><span class="font-mono text-white">1</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.37%"></div></div></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 items-center"><div><div class="flex justify-between mb-1 text-[12px]"><span class="font-mono text-gray-300">Wiki</span><span class="font-mono text-white">1</span></div><div class="w-full h-2 bg-white/[0.06] rounded-[2px] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-[2px] bg-slate-400/70" style="width:0.37%"></div></div></div></div></div><div class="mt-6"><div class="border-l-2 border-teal-500/40 pl-4 mb-6"><h3 id="aiis-filter" class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2 scroll-mt-20"><a href="#aiis-filter" class="hover:text-teal-300">Filter rendered HTML for the AIIS hidden injection signatures in agent retrieval pipelines.</a></h3><p class="text-sm text-gray-300 mb-2">Hidden text and HTML comments are where most of the bait lives, and the Unicode tag block class and the script literal placement are the ones that grew. An agent that pulls web content into its context without stripping hidden text, comments, script literals and tag block Unicode is reading the bait as instructions.</p><p class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-mono">Maps to:<!-- --> <span><a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-2002" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-2002</a></span> · <span><a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/3.1" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->3.1</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Prompt Injection Protection<!-- -->)</span></a></span><span>, <a href="https://oasb.ai/controls/3.3" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="font-mono">OASB <!-- -->3.3</span> <span class="text-gray-400">(<!-- -->Input Validation<!-- -->)</span></a></span></p></div></div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">Callback attribution by client class</h3><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">Verdicts over the <!-- -->2,813<!-- --> attributed callbacks, read from what each client declared about itself. <!-- -->140<!-- --> callbacks declared a named model vendor in their user agent, and a declaration is not an identity, because the string is attacker controllable. Page level attribution, as distinct from callback attribution, covers <!-- -->15,429<!-- --> of the<!-- --> <!-- -->340,018<!-- --> AgentPwn rows of every event type, so this report states no page level agent share.</p><div class="mb-4 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-6"><div class="md:w-48 shrink-0 flex justify-center"><div class="flex flex-col items-center"><svg width="180" height="180" viewBox="0 0 180 180" role="img" aria-label="distribution donut chart"><path d="M 90 12 A 78 78 0 1 1 50.91201904731197 22.5008907833422 L 65.76545180933343 48.15055228567217 A 48.36 48.36 0 1 0 90 41.64 Z" class="fill-rose-400/85"></path><path d="M 50.91201904731197 22.5008907833422 A 78 78 0 0 1 89.99999999999999 12 L 89.99999999999999 41.64 A 48.36 48.36 0 0 0 65.76545180933343 48.15055228567217 Z" class="fill-amber-400/85"></path><path d="M 89.99999999999999 12 A 78 78 0 0 1 89.99999999999999 12 L 89.99999999999999 41.64 A 48.36 48.36 0 0 0 89.99999999999999 41.64 Z" class="fill-slate-400/85"></path><path d="M 89.99999999999999 12 A 78 78 0 0 1 89.99999999999999 12 L 89.99999999999999 41.64 A 48.36 48.36 0 0 0 89.99999999999999 41.64 Z" class="fill-teal-400/85"></path><text x="90" y="90" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" class="fill-white" style="font-size:46.800000000000004px;font-family:var(--font-newsreader), Georgia, serif">0</text></svg><p class="mt-3 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 text-center max-w-[12rem] font-mono">declared autonomous agents</p></div></div><div class="flex-1 overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-sm rw-table-stack" data-label-look="body"><thead><tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 font-medium">Attribution category</th><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 font-medium">Share</th><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 font-medium">Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-white align-top"><tr class="border-b border-gray-800/60"><td class="py-2 px-3">Browsers and link prefetchers</td><td data-label="Share" class="py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 text-sm font-mono">91.6%</td><td data-label="Notes" class="py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 text-sm">Standard browser and mobile WebKit user agents, including link unfurlers and previewers. 2,578 of 2,813 attributed callbacks.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-gray-800/60"><td class="py-2 px-3">Declared LLM content crawlers</td><td data-label="Share" class="py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 text-sm font-mono">8.4%</td><td data-label="Notes" class="py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 text-sm">Clients declaring a crawler identity in their user agent. 235 of 2,813 attributed callbacks, 47 of them verified by network ownership. They fetch content; they don&#x27;t act on it.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-gray-800/60"><td class="py-2 px-3">Generic HTTP clients</td><td data-label="Share" class="py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 text-sm font-mono">0%</td><td data-label="Notes" class="py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 text-sm">Library user agents with no browser or crawler identity. 0 of 2,813 attributed callbacks this window.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-gray-800/60"><td class="py-2 px-3">Autonomous LLM agents</td><td data-label="Share" class="py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 text-sm font-mono">0%</td><td data-label="Notes" class="py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 text-sm">Agent runtimes acting on tool output. 0 of 2,813 attributed callbacks. The previous window found none on a full window of attribution.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class="border-l-2 border-teal-500/40 pl-4 mb-6"><h3 id="common-crawl-gap" class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2 scroll-mt-20"><a href="#common-crawl-gap" class="hover:text-teal-300">Close the Common Crawl gap by instrumenting authenticated and dynamic surfaces.</a></h3><p class="text-sm text-gray-300 mb-2">Public web crawls, including Google&#x27;s April 2026 indirect prompt injection study, can&#x27;t see login walled, per fingerprint dynamic or federated surfaces. Two full windows of callback attribution drew declared browsers and crawlers and no declared agents from the public web cohort. The surface that could observe an autonomous agent acting on an injection is the authenticated one no crawl reaches, which is why AgentPwn&#x27;s delta cohort exists, so instrument yours the same way before you draw conclusions about agents from crawl data.</p></div><h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">Agent Threat Matrix evidence tiers</h3><div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 items-center mb-6"><div class="md:w-1/3 flex justify-center"><div class="flex flex-col items-center"><svg width="180" height="180" viewBox="0 0 180 180" role="img" aria-label="distribution donut chart"><path d="M 90 12 A 78 78 0 0 1 167.7673670629851 96.01968604587843 L 138.21576757905075 93.73220534844462 A 48.36 48.36 0 0 0 90 41.64 Z" class="fill-emerald-400/85"></path><path d="M 167.7673670629851 96.01968604587843 A 78 78 0 1 1 66.27904307845355 15.694440297336172 L 75.2930067086412 43.93055298434843 A 48.36 48.36 0 1 0 138.21576757905075 93.73220534844462 Z" class="fill-teal-400/85"></path><path d="M 66.27904307845355 15.694440297336172 A 78 78 0 0 1 89.99999999999999 12 L 89.99999999999999 41.64 A 48.36 48.36 0 0 0 75.2930067086412 43.93055298434843 Z" class="fill-slate-400/85"></path><text x="90" y="90" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" class="fill-white" style="font-size:46.800000000000004px;font-family:var(--font-newsreader), Georgia, serif">61</text></svg><p class="mt-3 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 text-center max-w-[12rem] font-mono">techniques</p></div></div><div class="flex-1"><ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm"><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-emerald-400/85"></span><span class="text-gray-300 flex-1">Observed in production</span><span class="font-mono text-white">16</span></li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-teal-400/85"></span><span class="text-gray-300 flex-1">Validated in lab</span><span class="font-mono text-white">42</span></li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-slate-400/85"></span><span class="text-gray-300 flex-1">Adapted from published research</span><span class="font-mono text-white">3</span></li></ul><p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2">Source: <a href="https://threats.opena2a.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline">Agent Threat Matrix</a> <!-- -->evidence audit. The Registry serves the third tier as &quot;adapted&quot; and this edition follows the source.</p></div></div></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">Appendix B: First Observed In The Wild log</h2><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">FOITW is the mechanism by which OpenA2A pre registers signatures for sophisticated AI agent attack techniques and publishes within seven days of first wild observation. The pre registration catalog is held internally until transparency log anchoring lands, so until then the registration dates below are our claim and not an independently verifiable one. Full methodology at<!-- --> <a class="text-teal-300 hover:underline" href="/methodology/foitw">/methodology/foitw</a>.</p><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">Catalog state at measurement:<!-- --> <strong class="text-white">3</strong> signatures registered,<!-- --> <strong class="text-white">0</strong> firings during the reporting window.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4"><table class="w-full text-sm rw-table-stack" data-label-look="body"><thead><tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 font-medium">Catalog ID</th><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 font-medium">Name</th><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 font-medium">Technique</th><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 text-gray-300 font-medium">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-white"><tr class="border-b border-gray-800/60 align-top"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-mono text-xs">FOITW-CAT-0001</td><td data-label="Name" class="py-2 px-3">Greshake-class indirect prompt injection via web content<div class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Greshake et al. (AISec 2023). Not what you&#x27;ve signed up for: Compromising Real-World LLM-Integrated Applications with Indirect Prompt Injection.</div></td><td data-label="Technique" class="py-2 px-3"><a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-2002" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-2002</a></td><td data-label="Status" class="py-2 px-3 text-xs text-gray-300">Pre-registered <!-- -->2026-04-27<!-- -->. <!-- -->Not yet fired.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-gray-800/60 align-top"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-mono text-xs">FOITW-CAT-0002</td><td data-label="Name" class="py-2 px-3">Actor-Critic adaptive multi-turn manipulation<div class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Shi, Lin, Song, et al. Lessons from Defending Gemini Against Indirect Prompt Injections (Google DeepMind, 2025).</div></td><td data-label="Technique" class="py-2 px-3"><a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-2007" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-2007</a></td><td data-label="Status" class="py-2 px-3 text-xs text-gray-300">Pre-registered <!-- -->2026-04-27<!-- -->. <!-- -->Not yet fired.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-gray-800/60 align-top"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-mono text-xs">FOITW-CAT-0003</td><td data-label="Name" class="py-2 px-3">Reputation-poisoning prompt injection<div class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Brunner, Liu, Pande. AI threats in the wild: The current state of prompt injections on the web (Google Threat Intelligence Group, April 2026).</div></td><td data-label="Technique" class="py-2 px-3"><a href="https://threats.opena2a.org/techniques/T-9005" class="text-teal-300 hover:underline font-mono text-xs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T-9005</a></td><td data-label="Status" class="py-2 px-3 text-xs text-gray-300">Pre-registered <!-- -->2026-04-27<!-- -->. <!-- -->Not yet fired.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="mb-12"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">Appendix C: Live indices</h2><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">The three indices below update between editions. Sophistication is published as a distribution only: no mean, no grade, no month over month delta.</p><section class="mb-10 border border-white/10 rounded p-4 bg-white/[0.02]"><h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2 text-white">Live indices at publication</h3><p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mb-3">The numbers in this report are the time capsule snapshot; the indices below are continuously updated. Click through for the live methodology and CSV exports.</p><div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-sm"><a class="border border-white/10 rounded p-3 hover:border-teal-500/60 transition-colors" href="/indices/exposure-prevalence"><div class="text-xs text-gray-400">Exposure Prevalence Index</div><div class="text-lg font-bold text-white">ARIAscout</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-300 mt-1">Shodan sweeps</div></a><a class="border border-white/10 rounded p-3 hover:border-teal-500/60 transition-colors" href="/indices/attack-prevalence"><div class="text-xs text-gray-400">Attack Prevalence Index</div><div class="text-lg font-bold text-white">ARIAtrap</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-300 mt-1">Honeypot fleet behavioral data</div></a><a class="border border-white/10 rounded p-3 hover:border-teal-500/60 transition-colors" href="/indices/sophistication"><div class="text-xs text-gray-400">Sophistication Index</div><div class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Distribution-only</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-300 mt-1">Mean withheld pending classifier validation</div></a></div></section></section><div class="border-t border-gray-800 pt-6 text-xs text-gray-400 space-y-3"><p><strong class="text-white">Authorship.</strong> <!-- -->ARIA is OpenA2A&#x27;s autonomous research system. Editorial review by Abdel Fane. We document how our content is made.</p><p><strong class="text-white">Data integrity.</strong> Every value in this report traces to a query on live instrumentation, run in one pass on <!-- -->October 19, 2026<!-- --> with the window bounds fixed. The exposure sweep ran on the same date inside the pass, and the figures the continuity notes name were recounted on the same bounds in the same pass.</p><p><strong class="text-white">License.</strong> Apache 2.0. Cite using the BibTeX or APA blocks under Methodology.</p><p><strong class="text-white">Coordinated disclosure.</strong> Any finding in this report that maps to a previously undisclosed vulnerability is held under the 90-day ARIAdesk disclosure protocol. None of the surface level findings in this report require disclosure coordination.</p></div><section id="changes" aria-labelledby="changes-heading" data-changes="" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-12"><h2 id="changes-heading" class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">Changes to this report</h2><ol role="list" class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-4 *:scroll-mt-20 *:border-l-2 *:border-white/15 *:pl-4 *:text-sm *:leading-relaxed *:text-gray-300"><li id="erratum-previous-window-total" class="scroll-mt-20" data-correction=""><time dateTime="2026-10-27">October 27, 2026</time>. The note on autonomous agents in the Appendix A class table gave the previous window&#x27;s attributed callback total. Read with Issue 5&#x27;s class counts, it let a client class with one source be computed, and a figure about one source can single it out. The total is removed, and the note now says only that the previous window found none.<!-- --> <a class="text-teal-300 hover:underline" href="/reports/state-of-ai-agent-security-2026-09#erratum-withheld-class">Issue 5</a> <!-- -->carries a matching correction. No measured value changed.</li><li id="erratum-behaviour-breakdowns-withheld" class="scroll-mt-20">Erratum (<!-- -->2026-10-25<!-- -->): the comparisons with Issue 5&#x27;s tool call, MCP connection, A2A handshake and A2A task counts and with its A2A and automated scanner shares are withdrawn from the thesis, the summary, the search description, the opening paragraph, two cards in This month in numbers, key findings 1 and 3 and their sections, the chart title in section 1, the Bottom line, and an Appendix A note, with the clauses that rested on them. Issue 5 withdrew those figures: each needs ten or more distinct client addresses, and no count of them was on record when this edition was published, so that could not be confirmed. The reason given for the withheld breakdowns now reads &quot;could not be confirmed&quot; where it read &quot;has not been confirmed&quot;.           This edition&#x27;s own counts are unchanged.</li></ol></section></article></div><!--$--><!--/$--></main><footer class="border-t border-white/10" style="background:#06070a"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-10 sm:px-6"><nav aria-label="Footer" class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3"><div><p class="text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em]" style="font-family:var(--font-plex-mono), monospace;color:#5fd0c6">Research</p><ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm"><li><a